{
  "_comment": [
    "Canned HAL payloads for the emulator's default CMIS module (vendor xcvr-emu,",
    "PN EMU-40G-LR4, 40GBASE-LR4, 4 host / 4 media lanes) -- the uniform module the",
    "testbed presents on all in-use ports when EMU_NO_SPECIAL=1.",
    "",
    "Loaded byte-identically by the Rust and Python harnesses so both daemons are fed",
    "the same bytes. These are HAL-level payloads (what sonic_platform returns), NOT",
    "STATE_DB rows -- the daemon under test is what turns one into the other, and that",
    "transformation is precisely what is being benchmarked.",
    "",
    "dom_real_value carries 3 scalars + 8 lanes x 3 metrics = 27 fields, matching the",
    "reference field-count assertion (get_size_for_key('Ethernet0') == 27). Lanes 5-8",
    "read N/A on this 4-lane module, exactly as the emulator reports them.",
    "",
    "Refresh with tools/capture_fixture.sh against a live emulator rather than editing",
    "by hand, so the fixture cannot silently drift from what the DUT actually serves."
  ],

